SUMMARY:萬華萬象—共生與綻放「茶室文化主題走動式戲劇
 導覽」
DESCRIPTION:本場主題：青草綻放；國台語混合。\n\n萬華萬
 象—共生與綻放「茶室文化主題走動式戲劇導覽」 Wanhua
  in Many Colors: Coexisting & Flourishing — A Teahouse Culture Immersive
  Walking Theater Experience 推開茶室木門，走進被時光凝結的
 常民生活現場。這不僅是一場走讀導覽，更是一段融合
 角色演繹、感官互動與真實場域的文化體驗。邀您化身
 故事中的旅人，親身走進老城客廳，讀懂屬於萬華的生
 命記憶與溫暖日常。 Open the door to an old teahouse and step into
  everyday life from another time. This is more than a walking tour. It’s
  a cultural experience that brings together live performances\, sensory ex
 periences\, and real places in Wanhua. Join us as a traveler in the story\
 , step into Wanhua’s “living room\,” and discover the memories\, sto
 ries\, and everyday warmth of this old neighborhood. 🌿 主題一｜《
 青草綻放》（臺灣台語場） 自幼赴美的 Nancy，為了替住
 院的阿公祈福，重新踏上了這趟萬華歸鄉旅途。在導覽
 員的帶領下，觀眾將與 Nancy 一同從百年青草巷啟程，品
 飲青草茶、辨識草藥。隨後步入剝皮寮的紅磚木窗下，
 尋找昔日「老茶桌仔」遺留的歷史線索。在這趟充滿草
 藥清涼與歷史氣息的五感走讀中，Nancy 究竟會遇見誰？
 這趟尋根之旅，又將如何揭開萬華強韌的生活美學與在
 地真切的人情溫度？邀請您親自走入街區，一探究竟。 (
 青草綻放場次補充說明：兩場活動戲劇演出與導覽皆相
 同，演出以在地生活最真實的「國台語混合」自然呈現
 ，不懂深奧台語也能輕鬆融入，非常適合長輩或闔家同
 行！) 🍵 主題二｜《萬象品茗》（中英雙語場） 自幼赴
 美的 Nancy 為了探望生病的阿公重返萬華，邀請觀眾化身
 「茶友」，循著阿公常去的「金孔雀」、「艋舺茶館」
 與「牽手茶室」展開尋味之旅。旅途中 Nancy 意外重逢國
 小同學阿珠與美滿，在熟悉的老歌與茶香中，看見茶室
 女性為家計打拚的辛酸，也體會她們用溫暖陪伴老客人
 的真情—原來阿公念念不忘的不只是茶，更是「茶燒燒
 ，心嘛燒燒」的老城人情味。 (萬象品茗場次補充說明：
 兩場活動戲劇演出與導覽皆相同，劇中穿插「國台語與
 部分英文日常互動」，導覽則以「國台語混合」解說。10
 /4 中英文雙語場次特別為外國友人備有「英文戲劇導覽
 小卡」，無論是外國朋友或是想要帶外國友人體驗在地
 文化的民眾，都能瞭解萬華茶室文化！) 票務與參與資訊
  活動地點：萬華區街區與在地茶室 集合地點：捷運龍山
 寺站 活動場次：  【主題一｜青草綻放】 10/03 (六) 10:30-1
 2:00(臺灣台語場) 10/17 (六) 10:30-12:00 【主題二｜萬象品茗
 】 10/04 (日) 10:30-12:00 (中英雙語場) 10/18 (日) 10:30-12:00 票
 價資訊： 一般票：NT$ 250/人 愛心票：NT$ 150/人(65歲以上
 長者、1歲以下兒童) 親子套票：NT$ 300/組(1位成人及1位12
 歲以下兒童) 報名與活動注意事項 實名制與保險：為保
 障參與者權益，本活動全程投保公共意外責任險。購票
 報名時，請務必確實填寫參加者之真實中文姓名、身分
 證字號與出生年月日。 準時報到：請於活動開始前 10 分
 鐘抵達集合地點，領取導覽設備與聆聽行前說明，以利
 準時出發。 穿著與設備：活動全程需於街區步道與室內
 空間步行，建議穿著輕便衣物與好走的鞋子。 觀賞禮儀
 ：演出過程中包含演員實境互動，請配合現場引路人引
 導；為維持整體氛圍，進行中請避免大聲喧嘩。 意見回
 饋：活動尾聲將安排短暫交流，懇請參與者協助填寫回
 饋問卷，共同為萬華文化推廣提供寶貴建言。 退票規範
 ：本活動依照 ACCUPASS 平台退改政策辦理。活動當日因個
 人因素逾時未到或缺席者，恕不予退費。 如遇天然災害
 以致活動延期，本活動將「青草綻放」場次延期至10月24
 日舉辦；「萬象品茗」場次延期至10月25日舉辦。   Progra
 m Introduction & Storylines 🌿 Theme 1｜"Herbal Blooms" (Taiwanese Hokk
 ien Session) Nancy grew up in the United States. Now\, she returns to Wanh
 ua to pray for her grandfather\, who is in the hospital. Led by a local gu
 ide\, you’ll join Nancy on a journey through the century-old Herb Lane.
  Along the way\, you’ll taste herbal tea and learn about local medicinal
  plants. Then\, you’ll walk through Bopiliao Historic Block\, passing it
 s red-brick walls and wooden windows as you search for clues left behind b
 y the old tea stalls. Along this journey filled with the fresh scent of he
 rbs and the atmosphere of old Wanhua\, who will Nancy meet? And what will
  she discover about the resilience\, everyday beauty\, and human warmth of
  Wanhua? Come walk the streets with us and find out for yourself.  🍵 T
 heme 2｜"Tea & Stories of Wanhua" (Mandarin & English Bilingual Session)
  Nancy grew up in the United States and returns to Wanhua to visit her sic
 k grandfather. Join Nancy as a “tea companion” and follow the places h
 er grandfather used to visit\, including Golden Peacock\, Bangka Teahouse\
 , and Hand-in-Hand Teahouse. Along the way\, Nancy unexpectedly reunites w
 ith her old elementary school classmates\, Ah Zhu and Mei Man. As old song
 s play and the aroma of tea fills the air\, she learns about the struggles
  these teahouse women faced while supporting their families\, as well as t
 he warmth and companionship they shared with their longtime customers. Nan
 cy begins to understand that what her grandfather missed was not just the
  tea\, but the warmth of the people and the sense of community that made o
 ld Wanhua special. Event Info Locations: Wanhua historic neighborhood stre
 ets & local authentic teahouses Meeting Point: MRT Longshan Temple Station
  Session Schedule: 【Theme 1｜Herbal Blooms】 10/03 (Sat) 10:30–12:00
  (Taiwanese Hokkien Session) 10/17 (Sat) 10:30–12:00 (Herbal Blooms Note
 : Both sessions are exactly the same. The play and tour are in a natural m
 ix of Mandarin and Taiwanese\, just like real daily life here. You don’t
  need to know advanced Taiwanese to enjoy it—it's great for seniors and
  the whole family!) 【Theme 2｜Tea & Stories of Wanhua】 10/04 (Sun) 10
 :30–12:00 (Mandarin & English Bilingual Session) 10/18 (Sun) 10:30–12:
 00 (Tea & Stories of Wanhua Note: Both sessions are exactly the same. The
  actors chat naturally in a mix of Mandarin\, Taiwanese\, and some everyda
 y English\, while the tour itself is in Mandarin and Taiwanese. For the Oc
 t 4 bilingual session\, we have a handy English Guide Card ready for forei
 gn guests. Whether you're visiting from abroad or bringing friends from ov
 erseas\, everyone can easily follow along and enjoy Wanhua’s teahouse cu
 lture!)    Ticket Prices: General Ticket: NT$ 250 / person Concession Tic
 ket: NT$ 150 / person (seniors aged 65 and above and infants under 1 year
  old) Family Package: NT$ 300 / set (1 adult + 1 child under 12) Registrat
 ion & Insurance Insurance & Registration: Public liability insurance is in
 cluded for all participants. When signing up\, please make sure to provide
  each attendee’s full legal name\, ID/Passport number\, and date of birt
 h. Arrival Time: Please arrive at the meeting spot at least 10 minutes ear
 ly to pick up your audio gear and listen to a brief orientation so we can
  head out on time. What to Wear: We’ll be walking through outdoor alleys
  and visiting indoor teahouses. We strongly recommend wearing comfortable
  clothes and walking shoes. Tour Etiquette: This experience includes live\
 , interactive performances. Please follow your guide's directions and keep
  noise to a minimum so everyone can enjoy the immersive atmosphere. Feedba
 ck: We’ll have a brief wrap-up chat at the end. We’d love it if you co
 uld take a couple of minutes to fill out our quick survey and help us keep
  sharing Wanhua's culture! Refund Policy: Ticket changes and refunds follo
 w ACCUPASS policies. Unfortunately\, no refunds can be given for late arri
 vals or no-shows on the event day. Rescheduling Due to Severe Weather: If
  the event has to be postponed due to severe weather (such as a typhoon wa
 rning)\, Herbal Blooms will be rescheduled to October 24\, and Tea & Stori
 es of Wanhua will be rescheduled to October 25.   主辦單位：臺北
 市政府文化局 執行單位：閱野文創股份有限公司\n一般
 票250元；65歲以上及1歲以下150元；親子套票300元（1成人
 及1名12歲以下兒童）。\nhttps://www.accupass.com/event/26090913134
 29433024630
LOCATION:捷運龍山寺站集合；萬華區街區與在地茶室 台灣
 台北市萬華區富民里西園路一段153號
URL:https://www.accupass.com/event/2609091313429433024630
