SUMMARY:萬華萬象—共生與綻放「茶室文化主題走動式戲劇
 導覽」
DESCRIPTION:本場主題：萬象品茗；國台語混合、部分英文。
 \n\n萬華萬象—共生與綻放「茶室文化主題走動式戲劇導
 覽」 Wanhua in Many Colors: Coexisting & Flourishing — A Teahouse Cult
 ure Immersive Walking Theater Experience 推開茶室木門，走進被時
 光凝結的常民生活現場。這不僅是一場走讀導覽，更是
 一段融合角色演繹、感官互動與真實場域的文化體驗。
 邀您化身故事中的旅人，親身走進老城客廳，讀懂屬於
 萬華的生命記憶與溫暖日常。 Open the door to an old teahouse a
 nd step into everyday life from another time. This is more than a walking
  tour. It’s a cultural experience that brings together live performances
 \, sensory experiences\, and real places in Wanhua. Join us as a traveler
  in the story\, step into Wanhua’s “living room\,” and discover the
  memories\, stories\, and everyday warmth of this old neighborhood. 🌿
  主題一｜《青草綻放》（臺灣台語場） 自幼赴美的 Nancy
 ，為了替住院的阿公祈福，重新踏上了這趟萬華歸鄉旅
 途。在導覽員的帶領下，觀眾將與 Nancy 一同從百年青草
 巷啟程，品飲青草茶、辨識草藥。隨後步入剝皮寮的紅
 磚木窗下，尋找昔日「老茶桌仔」遺留的歷史線索。在
 這趟充滿草藥清涼與歷史氣息的五感走讀中，Nancy 究竟
 會遇見誰？這趟尋根之旅，又將如何揭開萬華強韌的生
 活美學與在地真切的人情溫度？邀請您親自走入街區，
 一探究竟。 (青草綻放場次補充說明：兩場活動戲劇演出
 與導覽皆相同，演出以在地生活最真實的「國台語混合
 」自然呈現，不懂深奧台語也能輕鬆融入，非常適合長
 輩或闔家同行！) 🍵 主題二｜《萬象品茗》（中英雙語
 場） 自幼赴美的 Nancy 為了探望生病的阿公重返萬華，邀
 請觀眾化身「茶友」，循著阿公常去的「金孔雀」、「
 艋舺茶館」與「牽手茶室」展開尋味之旅。旅途中 Nancy
  意外重逢國小同學阿珠與美滿，在熟悉的老歌與茶香中
 ，看見茶室女性為家計打拚的辛酸，也體會她們用溫暖
 陪伴老客人的真情—原來阿公念念不忘的不只是茶，更
 是「茶燒燒，心嘛燒燒」的老城人情味。 (萬象品茗場次
 補充說明：兩場活動戲劇演出與導覽皆相同，劇中穿插
 「國台語與部分英文日常互動」，導覽則以「國台語混
 合」解說。10/4 中英文雙語場次特別為外國友人備有「英
 文戲劇導覽小卡」，無論是外國朋友或是想要帶外國友
 人體驗在地文化的民眾，都能瞭解萬華茶室文化！) 票務
 與參與資訊 活動地點：萬華區街區與在地茶室 集合地點
 ：捷運龍山寺站 活動場次：  【主題一｜青草綻放】 10/0
 3 (六) 10:30-12:00(臺灣台語場) 10/17 (六) 10:30-12:00 【主題二
 ｜萬象品茗】 10/04 (日) 10:30-12:00 (中英雙語場) 10/18 (日) 1
 0:30-12:00 票價資訊： 一般票：NT$ 250/人 愛心票：NT$ 150/人
 (65歲以上長者、1歲以下兒童) 親子套票：NT$ 300/組(1位成
 人及1位12歲以下兒童) 報名與活動注意事項 實名制與保
 險：為保障參與者權益，本活動全程投保公共意外責任
 險。購票報名時，請務必確實填寫參加者之真實中文姓
 名、身分證字號與出生年月日。 準時報到：請於活動開
 始前 10 分鐘抵達集合地點，領取導覽設備與聆聽行前說
 明，以利準時出發。 穿著與設備：活動全程需於街區步
 道與室內空間步行，建議穿著輕便衣物與好走的鞋子。
  觀賞禮儀：演出過程中包含演員實境互動，請配合現場
 引路人引導；為維持整體氛圍，進行中請避免大聲喧嘩
 。 意見回饋：活動尾聲將安排短暫交流，懇請參與者協
 助填寫回饋問卷，共同為萬華文化推廣提供寶貴建言。
  退票規範：本活動依照 ACCUPASS 平台退改政策辦理。活動
 當日因個人因素逾時未到或缺席者，恕不予退費。 如遇
 天然災害以致活動延期，本活動將「青草綻放」場次延
 期至10月24日舉辦；「萬象品茗」場次延期至10月25日舉辦
 。   Program Introduction & Storylines 🌿 Theme 1｜"Herbal Blooms" (T
 aiwanese Hokkien Session) Nancy grew up in the United States. Now\, she re
 turns to Wanhua to pray for her grandfather\, who is in the hospital. Led
  by a local guide\, you’ll join Nancy on a journey through the century-o
 ld Herb Lane. Along the way\, you’ll taste herbal tea and learn about lo
 cal medicinal plants. Then\, you’ll walk through Bopiliao Historic Block
 \, passing its red-brick walls and wooden windows as you search for clues
  left behind by the old tea stalls. Along this journey filled with the fre
 sh scent of herbs and the atmosphere of old Wanhua\, who will Nancy meet?
  And what will she discover about the resilience\, everyday beauty\, and h
 uman warmth of Wanhua? Come walk the streets with us and find out for your
 self.  🍵 Theme 2｜"Tea & Stories of Wanhua" (Mandarin & English Bilin
 gual Session) Nancy grew up in the United States and returns to Wanhua to
  visit her sick grandfather. Join Nancy as a “tea companion” and follo
 w the places her grandfather used to visit\, including Golden Peacock\, Ba
 ngka Teahouse\, and Hand-in-Hand Teahouse. Along the way\, Nancy unexpecte
 dly reunites with her old elementary school classmates\, Ah Zhu and Mei Ma
 n. As old songs play and the aroma of tea fills the air\, she learns about
  the struggles these teahouse women faced while supporting their families\
 , as well as the warmth and companionship they shared with their longtime
  customers. Nancy begins to understand that what her grandfather missed wa
 s not just the tea\, but the warmth of the people and the sense of communi
 ty that made old Wanhua special. Event Info Locations: Wanhua historic nei
 ghborhood streets & local authentic teahouses Meeting Point: MRT Longshan
  Temple Station Session Schedule: 【Theme 1｜Herbal Blooms】 10/03 (Sat
 ) 10:30–12:00 (Taiwanese Hokkien Session) 10/17 (Sat) 10:30–12:00 (Her
 bal Blooms Note: Both sessions are exactly the same. The play and tour are
  in a natural mix of Mandarin and Taiwanese\, just like real daily life he
 re. You don’t need to know advanced Taiwanese to enjoy it—it's great f
 or seniors and the whole family!) 【Theme 2｜Tea & Stories of Wanhua】
  10/04 (Sun) 10:30–12:00 (Mandarin & English Bilingual Session) 10/18 (S
 un) 10:30–12:00 (Tea & Stories of Wanhua Note: Both sessions are exactly
  the same. The actors chat naturally in a mix of Mandarin\, Taiwanese\, an
 d some everyday English\, while the tour itself is in Mandarin and Taiwane
 se. For the Oct 4 bilingual session\, we have a handy English Guide Card r
 eady for foreign guests. Whether you're visiting from abroad or bringing f
 riends from overseas\, everyone can easily follow along and enjoy Wanhua
 ’s teahouse culture!)    Ticket Prices: General Ticket: NT$ 250 / perso
 n Concession Ticket: NT$ 150 / person (seniors aged 65 and above and infan
 ts under 1 year old) Family Package: NT$ 300 / set (1 adult + 1 child unde
 r 12) Registration & Insurance Insurance & Registration: Public liability
  insurance is included for all participants. When signing up\, please make
  sure to provide each attendee’s full legal name\, ID/Passport number\,
  and date of birth. Arrival Time: Please arrive at the meeting spot at lea
 st 10 minutes early to pick up your audio gear and listen to a brief orien
 tation so we can head out on time. What to Wear: We’ll be walking throug
 h outdoor alleys and visiting indoor teahouses. We strongly recommend wear
 ing comfortable clothes and walking shoes. Tour Etiquette: This experience
  includes live\, interactive performances. Please follow your guide's dire
 ctions and keep noise to a minimum so everyone can enjoy the immersive atm
 osphere. Feedback: We’ll have a brief wrap-up chat at the end. We’d lo
 ve it if you could take a couple of minutes to fill out our quick survey a
 nd help us keep sharing Wanhua's culture! Refund Policy: Ticket changes an
 d refunds follow ACCUPASS policies. Unfortunately\, no refunds can be give
 n for late arrivals or no-shows on the event day. Rescheduling Due to Seve
 re Weather: If the event has to be postponed due to severe weather (such a
 s a typhoon warning)\, Herbal Blooms will be rescheduled to October 24\, a
 nd Tea & Stories of Wanhua will be rescheduled to October 25.   主辦單
 位：臺北市政府文化局 執行單位：閱野文創股份有限公
 司\n一般票250元；65歲以上及1歲以下150元；親子套票300元
 （1成人及1名12歲以下兒童）。\nhttps://www.accupass.com/event/2
 609091313429433024630
LOCATION:捷運龍山寺站集合；萬華區街區與在地茶室 台灣
 台北市萬華區富民里西園路一段153號
